# Task 8 deployment evidence
# Captured 2026-08-22T08:10Z from C:\Users\Daniel\Documents\opencode\wifimic.

## Remote preflight and backend decision

Command:
    ssh arch-daniel "systemctl is-active iptables.service; systemctl is-active nftables.service; systemctl is-active ufw.service; test -f /etc/iptables/iptables.rules; test -f /etc/nftables.conf"

Result:
    iptables.service=inactive
    nftables.service=inactive
    ufw.service=active
    /etc/iptables/iptables.rules=present
    /etc/nftables.conf=present
    /usr/bin/iptables and /usr/bin/nft were present, but binary presence was not used for selection.

Decision: UFW is the active firewall manager and owns the iptables-nft ruleset. The selector therefore used the active UFW path, which is the only safe path on this host; it did not enable nftables.service beside UFW. The selector retains the required iptables-active, nftables-active, both-active abort, iptables-persistence abort, and neither-active nftables fallback branches.

## Unit installation and verification

Command:
    ssh arch-daniel "systemd-analyze --user verify ~/.config/systemd/user/wifimic-server.service"

Result:
    wifimic-server.service: Command /home/daniel/.local/bin/wifimic_server is not executable: No such file or directory
    verify_exit=1

The unit was installed at ~/.config/systemd/user/wifimic-server.service and uses systemd --user/default.target, `%h/.local/bin/wifimic_server`, and every hardening directive from the micdriver reference. The remote product binary is not installed yet (the server implementation is a later task), so a sustained active-service result cannot be honestly claimed. A bounded start probe showed `status=203/EXEC` and the service was stopped/reset-failed afterward.

## Firewall happy path

Command:
    scp deploy/systemd/wifimic-server.service deploy/linux/wifimic-server-firewall.sh deploy/linux/wifimic-server-iptables.sh deploy/linux/wifimic-server.nft arch-daniel:/tmp/
    ssh arch-daniel "sudo bash /tmp/wifimic-server-firewall.sh"
    powershell -NoProfile -EncodedCommand <UDP datagram to 192.168.0.210:6902 from local 192.168.0.200>
    ssh arch-daniel "sudo nft list chain ip filter ufw-user-input"

Result:
    UFW inserted `6902/udp ALLOW IN 192.168.0.200` followed by `6902/udp DENY IN Anywhere`; UFW default incoming policy is deny.
    ip saddr 192.168.0.200 udp dport 6902 counter packets 1 bytes 38 accept
    udp dport 6902 counter packets 0 bytes 0 drop
    The one accepted counter increment proves the permitted peer/port scope.
